---
/**
 * PLACEHOLDER - deliberately not wired to anything.
 *
 * WRMD and ShelterManager both publish running totals of real activity, and it
 * reads as far more honest than a wall of customer logos: the number starts
 * wherever it truly starts, including small, and it goes up on its own.
 *
 * ARK has no organizations yet, so there is no number. The rule this component
 * exists to enforce is that we do not invent one, and do not "round up from
 * beta". Wire it when the figures are real:
 *
 *   1. Add an unauthenticated aggregate endpoint to the ARK API that returns
 *      org-count, animal-count and log-count across all organizations. It must
 *      expose totals only - never a per-organization breakdown, and never
 *      anything that identifies a facility.
 *   2. Fetch it at build time in this component's frontmatter and let the
 *      nightly deploy be what refreshes it, so the page stays a static file
 *      with no client JavaScript.
 *   3. Print the retrieved-at date beside the figures. A stale counter that
 *      admits its age is honest; one that implies real-time is not.
 *   4. Delete this block and the `isPlaceholder` branch below.
 */
const isPlaceholder = true;

const metrics = [
  { label: "Organizations keeping records in ARK", note: "no organizations yet" },
  { label: "Animals under care", note: "no animals yet" },
  { label: "Entries written at an enclosure", note: "no entries yet" },
];
---

<div class="reveal rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-border bg-card p-7 sm:p-9">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
    <h3 class="text-xl">ARK in numbers</h3>
    {
      isPlaceholder && (
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-muted-foreground uppercase">
          Placeholder - not yet live
        </p>
      )
    }
  </div>

  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-muted-foreground">
    When there are real totals here they will be the real ones, published from the running system
    and dated. Until an organization is actually using ARK, the honest number is none, so that is
    what this says.
  </p>

  <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-3">
    {
      metrics.map((metric) => (
        <div class="border-t border-border pt-5">
          <dt class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{metric.label}</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-muted-foreground">
            <span aria-hidden="true">&ndash;</span>
            <span class="sr-only">{metric.note}</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>
</div>
